# Time zone of the camera: a POSIX TZ string, on the first line that is not
# a comment. Used for the clock in logs, cron jobs (scheduled reboot) and the
# image overlay.
#
# POSIX sign: the offset is what you ADD to local time to get UTC, so places
# east of Greenwich are negative. Examples:
#   UTC0                              UTC (default)
#   CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3        France, Belgium, Germany… (summer time included)
#   GMT0BST,M3.5.0/1,M10.5.0          United Kingdom
#   EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0            US Eastern
#   <+0530>-5:30                      India
UTC0
